course: dictionary
lesson: 9765
title: Holding it back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To suppress something means to stop it or hold it down. Often you suppress a feeling, like a laugh, a yawn or a sneeze, so that nobody notices it. «Ella had to suppress a giggle during the serious assembly.» The clues are serious assembly: Ella would not want to be noticed laughing, so she held the giggle back.
explain: Suppress can also mean stopping something by force. In history, rulers suppressed protests and rebellions. In Alice in Wonderland, the officers suppress the cheering guinea-pigs, and the story ends with Alice's cry, «Come, that finished the guinea-pigs!» Stopping by force is a much bigger thing than holding back a yawn.
explain: Suppress can also mean keeping something secret, or stopping something from growing or working. Medicine can suppress a cough, and firefighters suppress fires. To check your meaning, swap in a word such as stop or hold back. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: To suppress something means to stop it or hold it down.
fact: You can suppress a feeling, such as a laugh, a yawn or a sneeze.
fact: Rulers can suppress a rebellion or a protest by force.
fact: Suppress can mean to keep information secret so people cannot know it.
fact: Suppress can mean to stop a fire, an illness or a cough from growing or working.
exercise: «Ella had to suppress a giggle during the serious assembly.» What does suppress mean here? | Write it down carefully | Stop yourself from showing it | *Let it out loudly | Dance to it
exercise: «The king's soldiers suppressed the rebellion.» What does suppressed mean? | Helped the rebels to win | Sang about it loudly | Forgot all about it | *Stopped by force
exercise: «The firefighters soon suppressed the blaze.» Find and copy one word that means put out or stopped. | *suppressed | firefighters | soon | blaze
test: «The doctor said the medicine would suppress my cough.» What does suppress mean here? | Forget it ever happened | Ask someone about it | *Stop it from working | Make it louder
test: The minister tried to suppress the report, so the public would never read it. What does suppress mean here? | Read it aloud to the class | *Keep it secret | Print it in every newspaper | Make it longer
exam: Which sentence uses suppress to mean hold back a yawn? | Ravi tried to suppress a yawn during the long maths lesson. | The rebels will suppress the new laws. | The fire was suppressed by the rain, not by people. | *Tom tried to suppress a yawn in the long, boring film.
